1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,941
A heavy door is slow to start swinging.

2
00:00:02,941 --> 00:00:06,288
A merry-go-round full of
children is hard to get turning.

3
00:00:06,288 --> 00:00:08,881
But a small top spins up with one flick.

4
00:00:09,281 --> 00:00:12,206
Some things fight being
turned much more than others.

5
00:00:12,656 --> 00:00:15,138
Diya twirls a metre ruler in the lab.

6
00:00:15,138 --> 00:00:17,610
Held at its middle, it spins easily.

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:21,040
Held at one end, it is
suddenly hard to swing.

8
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:21,940
Same ruler.

9
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:22,812
Same mass.

10
00:00:22,736 --> 00:00:23,902
So what changed?

11
00:00:24,402 --> 00:00:26,821
The answer is called moment of inertia.

12
00:00:27,421 --> 00:00:28,774
First, plain inertia.

13
00:00:28,774 --> 00:00:31,113
A heavy trolley is hard to start moving.

14
00:00:31,113 --> 00:00:33,230
Its mass resists a change in motion.

15
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:35,804
Turning has its own kind of inertia.

16
00:00:35,804 --> 00:00:39,884
It tells you how hard it is to
start, or stop, something spinning.

17
00:00:40,284 --> 00:00:44,734
It depends on the mass, and also on
how far that mass sits from the axis,

18
00:00:44,734 --> 00:00:46,336
the line it turns about.

19
00:00:46,736 --> 00:00:52,229
For tiny bits of mass, moment of inertia,
I, equals the sum of m r squared.

20
00:00:52,229 --> 00:00:54,965
Its unit is the kilogram metre squared.

21
00:00:55,565 --> 00:00:58,043
Our motion notebook, seen from above.

22
00:00:58,043 --> 00:01:02,487
A light rod, one metre long, with
a one kilogram ball at each end.

23
00:01:02,837 --> 00:01:04,593
Spin it about its middle.

24
00:01:04,593 --> 00:01:07,315
Each ball is half a metre from the axis.

25
00:01:07,315 --> 00:01:10,134
So I is one times point two five, twice.

26
00:01:10,134 --> 00:01:11,034
Point five.

27
00:01:11,431 --> 00:01:13,370
Give it one joule of energy.

28
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:15,705
It turns at two radians per second.

29
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:17,157
Slow-mo replay.

30
00:01:17,157 --> 00:01:18,057
Freeze.

31
00:01:18,156 --> 00:01:20,427
Each ball moves along a circle.

32
00:01:20,427 --> 00:01:22,487
Its speed is r times omega.

33
00:01:22,487 --> 00:01:24,274
Half a metre times two.

34
00:01:24,274 --> 00:01:25,893
One metre per second.

35
00:01:26,293 --> 00:01:30,125
Now slide the axis toward one
end, keeping that one joule.

36
00:01:30,125 --> 00:01:32,045
Watch I climb on the graph.

37
00:01:32,445 --> 00:01:35,270
At the end, one ball sits on the axis.

38
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:37,519
The other is a full metre away.

39
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:38,673
I is now one.

40
00:01:38,673 --> 00:01:39,573
Double.

41
00:01:39,741 --> 00:01:44,302
The same one joule now gives only one
point four one radians per second.

42
00:01:44,302 --> 00:01:46,558
The far ball does all the moving.

43
00:01:47,158 --> 00:01:50,962
So, is moment of inertia fixed
for a body, like its mass?

44
00:01:50,962 --> 00:01:52,174
Pause and decide.

45
00:01:55,274 --> 00:01:56,174
No!

46
00:01:55,693 --> 00:01:57,243
It depends on the axis.

47
00:01:57,243 --> 00:02:00,762
Same rod, same mass, but I
doubled when the axis moved.

48
00:02:01,362 --> 00:02:03,522
Where does m r squared come from?

49
00:02:03,522 --> 00:02:05,765
From kinetic energy, step by step.

50
00:02:06,115 --> 00:02:07,015
Step one.

51
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:12,213
A bit of mass m, at a distance r from
the axis, moves at speed v equals

52
00:02:12,213 --> 00:02:13,113
r omega.

53
00:02:13,795 --> 00:02:14,695
Step two.

54
00:02:14,608 --> 00:02:17,265
Its kinetic energy is half m v squared.

55
00:02:17,265 --> 00:02:19,922
That is half m r squared omega squared.

56
00:02:20,672 --> 00:02:21,572
Step three.

57
00:02:21,519 --> 00:02:22,754
Add up every bit.

58
00:02:22,754 --> 00:02:26,651
All the bits share the same
omega, so take it outside the sum.

59
00:02:27,401 --> 00:02:28,301
Step four.

60
00:02:28,259 --> 00:02:32,679
K equals half, times the sum of
m r squared, times omega squared.

61
00:02:32,679 --> 00:02:33,853
That sum is I.

62
00:02:34,603 --> 00:02:37,148
So K equals half I omega squared.

63
00:02:37,148 --> 00:02:41,175
Just like half m v squared,
with I in place of mass.

64
00:02:41,775 --> 00:02:42,861
Remember this.

65
00:02:42,861 --> 00:02:46,150
Moment of inertia is the
turning version of mass.

66
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,515
I equals the sum of m r squared.

67
00:02:49,215 --> 00:02:52,208
Now, why the end is harder, link by link.

68
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:55,922
About the end, the far ball
swings round a big circle.

69
00:02:56,322 --> 00:03:00,124
A bigger circle in the same
time means a bigger speed.

70
00:03:00,124 --> 00:03:01,536
v equals r omega.

71
00:03:01,936 --> 00:03:04,446
Kinetic energy grows with speed squared.

72
00:03:04,446 --> 00:03:06,331
So it grows with r squared.

73
00:03:06,731 --> 00:03:08,997
So the same spin needs more energy.

74
00:03:08,997 --> 00:03:11,264
That is a bigger moment of inertia.

75
00:03:11,864 --> 00:03:12,952
Side by side.

76
00:03:12,952 --> 00:03:17,629
Two one kilogram balls, close in,
a tenth of a metre from the axis.

77
00:03:17,629 --> 00:03:19,191
I is point zero two.

78
00:03:19,591 --> 00:03:22,671
The same two balls, pushed
out to half a metre.

79
00:03:22,671 --> 00:03:23,875
I is point five.

80
00:03:23,875 --> 00:03:26,750
Twenty five times bigger,
with the same mass.

81
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:28,429
Now you try.

82
00:03:28,429 --> 00:03:33,407
If every ball moves twice as far from
the axis, does I become two times,

83
00:03:33,407 --> 00:03:35,020
or four times bigger?

84
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,362
Pause and decide.

85
00:03:39,562 --> 00:03:40,462
Four times!

86
00:03:40,459 --> 00:03:41,512
r is squared.

87
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:45,168
Twice the distance means four
times the moment of inertia.

88
00:03:45,819 --> 00:03:47,509
Now, one worked example.

89
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:52,619
A light rod has a one kilogram ball
point two metres from the axis, and

90
00:03:52,619 --> 00:03:55,599
a two kilogram ball
point five metres away.

91
00:03:55,599 --> 00:03:58,103
It spins at ten radians per second.

92
00:03:58,103 --> 00:04:00,442
Find I, and its kinetic energy.

93
00:04:00,942 --> 00:04:05,700
I equals one times point two squared,
plus two times point five squared.

94
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:09,078
That is point zero four plus point five.

95
00:04:09,078 --> 00:04:11,542
Point five four kilogram metre squared.

96
00:04:12,292 --> 00:04:16,081
K equals half, times point
five four, times ten squared.

97
00:04:16,081 --> 00:04:17,489
Twenty seven joules.

98
00:04:18,139 --> 00:04:19,600
Now, the exam trap.

99
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:22,499
Many students measure r
from the centre of the body.

100
00:04:22,899 --> 00:04:27,259
But r is the perpendicular
distance from the axis of rotation.

101
00:04:27,259 --> 00:04:30,107
Change the axis, and every r changes.

102
00:04:30,757 --> 00:04:32,256
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:32,256 --> 00:04:37,297
In finding I for a set of point masses,
and in using half I omega squared.

104
00:04:37,897 --> 00:04:39,091
Exam level now.

105
00:04:39,091 --> 00:04:43,796
Four two kilogram balls sit at the
corners of a light square frame of side

106
00:04:43,796 --> 00:04:44,696
one metre.

107
00:04:44,676 --> 00:04:49,522
Find the moment of inertia about an
axis through one corner, at right angles

108
00:04:49,522 --> 00:04:50,666
to the square.

109
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:51,910
Pause and solve.

110
00:04:57,310 --> 00:04:58,606
The answer is C.

111
00:04:58,606 --> 00:05:00,554
Eight kilogram metre squared.

112
00:05:01,054 --> 00:05:03,176
The ball on the axis adds nothing.

113
00:05:03,676 --> 00:05:05,765
Two balls are one metre away.

114
00:05:05,765 --> 00:05:08,006
Each adds two times one squared.

115
00:05:08,006 --> 00:05:08,906
Two each.

116
00:05:09,338 --> 00:05:11,909
The far ball is root two metres away.

117
00:05:11,909 --> 00:05:14,579
It adds two times two, which is four.

118
00:05:14,579 --> 00:05:15,695
Total, eight.

119
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:17,835
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:17,835 --> 00:05:19,418
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:22,618 --> 00:05:24,556
Can you answer these without help?

122
00:05:24,956 --> 00:05:25,856
One.

123
00:05:25,407 --> 00:05:29,282
Why is a ruler harder to spin about
its end than about its middle?

124
00:05:30,182 --> 00:05:31,082
Two.

125
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:35,167
If every mass moves twice as far
from the axis, what happens to I?

126
00:05:36,067 --> 00:05:36,967
Three.

127
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:40,720
Why is moment of inertia not
fixed for a body, the way mass is?

128
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:45,513
Next time: a ring and a
disc, same mass, same push.

129
00:05:45,513 --> 00:05:47,429
Which one spins up faster?

130
00:05:47,429 --> 00:05:48,858
Radius of gyration.
